Bullies are the worst.

254
00:23:36,041 --> 00:23:38,502
Do you have any idea how that feels?

255
00:23:40,045 --> 00:23:42,005
Mom!

256
00:23:43,423 --> 00:23:45,425
We're sorry.

257
00:23:45,509 --> 00:23:49,137
Do you?

258
00:24:05,863 --> 00:24:07,155
Ow, ow, ow...

259
00:24:16,915 --> 00:24:20,127
My friend, she's willing
to get on her knees to...

260
00:24:20,210 --> 00:24:24,006
She wants to beg for forgiveness.
She's clearly very remorseful. Right?

261
00:24:24,089 --> 00:24:25,841
- Yes.
- Yes.

262
00:24:27,426 --> 00:24:28,552
Well...

263
00:24:29,636 --> 00:24:30,470
That's enough. You can go.

264
00:24:30,554 --> 00:24:34,433
Oh, you're so incredibly generous.

265
00:24:34,516 --> 00:24:36,518
No, I, I...

266
00:24:37,394 --> 00:24:38,770
You should head inside.

267
00:24:38,854 --> 00:24:40,939
You. You!

268
00:24:41,023 --> 00:24:42,858
Hey, let go of me!

269
00:24:43,859 --> 00:24:44,818
What?

270
00:24:45,527 --> 00:24:47,529
Anger management issues
from not being able to find a job?

271
00:24:49,114 --> 00:24:50,490
Someone who works at SE?

272
00:24:50,574 --> 00:24:51,909
Do you know her?

273
00:24:54,494 --> 00:24:56,246
Never seen her before in my life.

274
00:24:56,330 --> 00:24:57,164
I know.

275
00:24:58,081 --> 00:24:58,999
I should've got her number.

276
00:25:00,083 --> 00:25:01,168
Hey, hurry, hurry!

277
00:25:02,753 --> 00:25:04,213
Hey, wait. Oh, hold on.

278
00:25:05,631 --> 00:25:09,885
Throw her! Wow, geez. Ah! Oh, man.

279
00:25:09,968 --> 00:25:12,763
- Oh, man.
- Ugh, she's heavy.

280
00:25:12,846 --> 00:25:14,306
Hey, what the... Geez.

281
00:25:14,389 --> 00:25:17,518
She weighs twice as much when she's drunk.
Seriously. Geez.

282
00:25:20,521 --> 00:25:22,814
Wow, I can't believe... Ugh.

283
00:25:26,068 --> 00:25:26,902
Hey.

284
00:25:27,653 --> 00:25:31,698
Wow, but for real, our Nam Da-reum
is actually becoming a successful fan.

285
00:25:33,158 --> 00:25:34,826
But do you think Chan knows?

286
00:25:34,910 --> 00:25:36,912
It's been ten years since DNX disbanded.

287
00:25:36,995 --> 00:25:39,373
That a fan from the Stone Age like her
still exists?

288
00:25:40,123 --> 00:25:41,458
I know, right?

289
00:25:41,542 --> 00:25:44,253
Hey, let's go too.

290
00:25:44,336 --> 00:25:45,295
Okay.

291
00:25:46,964 --> 00:25:47,965
Hey, wait, hold on.

292
00:25:51,260 --> 00:25:52,636
Seriously, go.

293
00:26:41,351 --> 00:26:42,811
SEONGJU STATION

294
00:26:48,108 --> 00:26:50,068
SEONGJU

295
00:26:57,826 --> 00:26:59,286
APPELLO

296
00:27:37,157 --> 00:27:39,535
- Which department did you join?
- Oh, uh, I'm in the MD Team.

297
00:27:40,244 --> 00:27:41,078
Um...

298
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:44,248
Oh, I'm in the Marketing Team.

299
00:27:44,331 --> 00:27:46,792
- Marketing? I'm in the Marketing Team too.
- Oh, really?

300
00:27:46,875 --> 00:27:50,212
Let's get along. I'm Park Youngwoo.

301
00:27:50,295 --> 00:27:54,132
- And your name is...?
- Oh, my name is Lee Min-a.

302
00:27:54,216 --> 00:27:55,050
- Ah, Min-a.
- Ms. Lee Min-a.

303
00:27:55,717 --> 00:27:56,802
Oh, I'm Nam Da-reum.

304
00:27:56,885 --> 00:27:59,638
Ms. Nam Da-reum.
So you're "one of a kind."

305
00:27:59,721 --> 00:28:00,889
Ah, yes. I get it.

306
00:28:01,890 --> 00:28:03,225
Let's all get along.

307
00:28:03,892 --> 00:28:05,394
"Love for your peers
is love for your country,"

308
00:28:05,477 --> 00:28:07,646
- as they say, right? How about a cheer?
- Oh, sounds good.

309
00:28:09,064 --> 00:28:10,190
Are you all friends already?

310
00:28:13,277 --> 00:28:16,196
Congratulations on becoming part of
the APPELLO family.

311
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:17,823
I'll be in charge of
your orientation today.

312
00:28:17,906 --> 00:28:22,619
I'm Kim Mi-young,
the manager of the Marketing Team.

313
00:28:22,703 --> 00:28:24,454
And these are your employee ID cards.

314
00:28:25,956 --> 00:28:27,875
- Mr. Youngwoo.
- Yes, thank you.

315
00:28:27,958 --> 00:28:29,585
- Ms. Min-a.
- Thank you.

316
00:28:29,668 --> 00:28:31,170
And Ms. Da-reum.

317
00:28:33,922 --> 00:28:34,882
Thank you.

318
00:28:35,549 --> 00:28:38,177
APPELLO currently has 82 employees.

319
00:28:38,260 --> 00:28:39,636
As of today, there are three new recruits.

320
00:28:39,720 --> 00:28:43,056
Then that means there are only 85
of these ID cards in the whole world.

321
00:28:43,140 --> 00:28:45,851
It's basically limited edition
merch from Chan.

322
00:28:46,896 --> 00:28:49,357
And it's even customized.

323
00:28:50,439 --> 00:28:53,275
All right, shall we begin
the proper company introduction now?

324
00:28:54,026 --> 00:28:55,319
- Let's go.
- Yes.

325
00:28:55,402 --> 00:28:56,653
- Yes.
- This way.

326
00:28:56,737 --> 00:28:58,322
Huh?

327
00:28:59,698 --> 00:29:02,367
- Please come this way.
- Okay.

328
00:29:08,624 --> 00:29:10,542
It's so clean and pretty.

329
00:29:12,252 --> 00:29:14,671
- Ah, Ms. Min-a.
- Ah.

330
00:29:15,339 --> 00:29:18,258
Most of the brands at APPELLO
are primarily online.

331
00:29:18,342 --> 00:29:20,469
So we run a pop-up showroom
on the first floor

332
00:29:20,552 --> 00:29:21,845
for them to meet customers.

333
00:29:23,972 --> 00:29:25,849
We also have spaces for our brands,

334
00:29:25,933 --> 00:29:28,393
like sewing rooms, pattern rooms,
and studios.

335
00:29:29,394 --> 00:29:32,231
Oh, and as you can see,
the dress code is casual.

336
00:29:32,314 --> 00:29:34,149
Starting tomorrow, you can wear
whatever fits your style,

337
00:29:34,233 --> 00:29:36,318
whether it's a swimsuit or a party dress.

338
00:29:36,401 --> 00:29:38,070
Wow.

339
00:29:45,827 --> 00:29:48,288
This is the studio where we shoot
lookbooks and campaigns.

340
00:29:48,372 --> 00:29:51,875
You could say all of APPELLO's
visual content comes from here.

341
00:30:13,063 --> 00:30:16,400
The Marketing Team and the MD Team
are on the fourth floor.

342
00:30:18,610 --> 00:30:20,237
Oh, and the CEO's office.

343
00:30:24,199 --> 00:30:28,495
- Lastly, let's go say hello to the CEO.
- What?

344
00:30:28,579 --> 00:30:30,455
- Right now?
- Yes.

345
00:30:44,887 --> 00:30:47,681
Hello. I'm the new employee, Nam Da-reum.

346
00:30:48,932 --> 00:30:50,184
That's so cheesy.

347
00:30:53,395 --> 00:30:56,607
- Nice to meet you. I'm Nam Da-reum.
- I'm Nam Da-reum.

348
00:30:57,524 --> 00:30:58,942
You sound like a call center.

349
00:31:00,402 --> 00:31:03,989
Just be normal.
And don't get nervous in front of Chan.

350
00:31:05,115 --> 00:31:06,491
Here, my secret weapon.

351
00:31:11,330 --> 00:31:13,290
They say this Herbal Calming Pill
helps with the nerves.

352
00:31:14,791 --> 00:31:16,043
Herbal Calming Pill... Her...

353
00:31:24,051 --> 00:31:25,677
Don't worry. Don't worry.

354
00:31:26,512 --> 00:31:29,556
I will send you the final proposal
by tomorrow morning.

355
00:31:30,224 --> 00:31:31,517
Thank you. Thank you.

356
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,560
CEO.

357
00:31:34,603 --> 00:31:36,355
These are our new employees.

358
00:31:42,861 --> 00:31:46,156
- Nice to meet you.
- I'm a new employee! I'm Park Youngwoo.

359
00:31:47,115 --> 00:31:48,534
Nice to meet you.

360
00:31:48,617 --> 00:31:50,827
Yes, I'm the new employee, Lee Min-a!

361
00:31:51,578 --> 00:31:52,579
That's me.

362
00:32:02,297 --> 00:32:03,298
Nice to meet you.

363
00:32:21,692 --> 00:32:24,444
Chan?

364
00:32:31,577 --> 00:32:35,122
What? Huh? Why is it someone else?

365
00:32:39,209 --> 00:32:40,752
I'm Nam Da-reum.

366
00:32:41,962 --> 00:32:43,213
NAM DA-REUM

367
00:32:47,593 --> 00:32:49,636
A sincere welcome to APPELLO.

368
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:53,265
My office door is always open,
so you're welcome anytime.

369
00:32:53,348 --> 00:32:56,393
Don't be formal.
Please treat me as a colleague.

370
00:32:56,476 --> 00:32:58,437
Let's do great things together.

371
00:32:58,520 --> 00:33:00,355
- Yes!
- Yes!

372
00:33:00,439 --> 00:33:03,150
All right, I think that's all.
Shall we head out?

373
00:33:03,233 --> 00:33:05,319
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

374
00:33:11,283 --> 00:33:13,744
It's him.

375
00:33:29,134 --> 00:33:30,719
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

376
00:33:36,517 --> 00:33:40,812
Da-reum, what's wrong?
Are you okay? Hey, breathe!

377
00:33:40,896 --> 00:33:41,897
- Call 911.
- Can't she breathe? What's wrong?

378
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:43,273
- Something's in her throat.
- She's choking.

379
00:33:43,357 --> 00:33:45,108
Try to breathe like this,
breathe, breathe...

380
00:33:45,192 --> 00:33:47,194
- What's wrong?
- Try to take a breath!

381
00:33:47,277 --> 00:33:48,529
Try to take a breath, breathe.

382
00:34:04,711 --> 00:34:07,381
Oh my! Oh my!

383
00:34:22,271 --> 00:34:24,356
Da-reum...

384
00:34:24,439 --> 00:34:26,233
Are you okay?

385
00:34:26,316 --> 00:34:27,276
She'll be all right now.

386
00:34:28,318 --> 00:34:29,987
I don't know what she ate, though.

387
00:34:31,947 --> 00:34:33,073
- No...
- What is this?

388
00:34:33,156 --> 00:34:33,991
What is this?

389
00:34:55,220 --> 00:34:56,722
Take care.

390
00:34:56,847 --> 00:34:59,808
Okay, okay, okay, okay, scoop, scoop!
Hey, guys, did you hear?

391
00:34:59,892 --> 00:35:03,228
They say the new hire, Nam Da-reum,
caused a huge scene on her first day.

392
00:35:03,312 --> 00:35:06,565
Seriously, a rookie causing trouble
on her first day.

393
00:35:08,483 --> 00:35:10,152
What?

394
00:35:14,823 --> 00:35:16,658
Mr. Lee Jin-sang?

395
00:35:20,746 --> 00:35:22,414
Oops.

396
00:35:22,497 --> 00:35:23,457
My mistake.

397
00:35:26,668 --> 00:35:27,920
Get back to work.

398
00:35:31,924 --> 00:35:34,635
I threw up on Director Lee Chan's pants
at my first company dinner.

399
00:35:37,930 --> 00:35:40,557
Anyone can make mistakes
when they're nervous.

400
00:35:40,641 --> 00:35:41,683
So don't worry about it too much.

401
00:35:44,228 --> 00:35:46,772
Thank you, Ms. Kim.

402
00:35:49,858 --> 00:35:52,611
Um, but...

403
00:35:52,694 --> 00:35:56,406
Wasn't Lee Chan supposed to be the CEO?

404
00:35:56,490 --> 00:35:59,368
They used to be co-CEOs.

405
00:35:59,451 --> 00:36:02,704
But it recently changed
to a single-CEO system.

406
00:36:02,788 --> 00:36:03,956
Then...

407
00:36:04,039 --> 00:36:06,208
Director Lee Chan is only in charge
of fashion directing

408
00:36:06,291 --> 00:36:07,543
for APPELLO's major events.

409
00:36:11,380 --> 00:36:12,381
I see.

410
00:36:24,393 --> 00:36:27,104
- So? So? You finally saw him in person?
- You weren't nervous, right?

411
00:36:28,063 --> 00:36:31,400
- ...
- Looks like you cried. Totally moved?

412
00:36:31,483 --> 00:36:33,402
We have to throw a party.
You're a successful fan!

413
00:36:33,485 --> 00:36:35,320
- What do you want to eat?
- Deal, deal, deal.

414
00:36:35,404 --> 00:36:37,114
Today, let's eat whatever
Da-reum wants to eat.

415
00:36:37,197 --> 00:36:39,199
- Deal!
- Deal! Deal!

416
00:36:39,283 --> 00:36:40,117
Deal!

417
00:36:41,451 --> 00:36:42,452
Guys.

418
00:36:43,203 --> 00:36:44,413
At Chan's company,

419
00:36:45,122 --> 00:36:46,748
Chan isn't there.

420
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:50,002
Huh? That's like a push-up bra
with no push.

421
00:36:50,127 --> 00:36:51,753
That one has 4 cm of super padding.

422
00:36:52,462 --> 00:36:56,341
- It'll really fill you out.
- Yes. In that case, can I get every color?

423
00:36:56,425 --> 00:36:57,718
And on top of that...

424
00:36:58,385 --> 00:37:01,680
- Huh?
- On my first day, a CEO hugged me.

425
00:37:01,763 --> 00:37:03,140
What?

426
00:37:04,808 --> 00:37:06,643
What kind of... plot twist is this?

427
00:37:08,645 --> 00:37:10,856
I'm so screwed!

428
00:37:21,408 --> 00:37:24,161
So you're telling me that
the person who face-planted

429
00:37:24,244 --> 00:37:27,414
on the CEO's chest was Nam Da-reum?

430
00:37:27,497 --> 00:37:31,251
And the fact that she's from
SE Corporation, especially now.

431
00:37:31,335 --> 00:37:32,836
It feels really sketchy, doesn't it?

432
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:35,422
If she'd put that on her resume,
even I wouldn't have hired her.

433
00:37:35,923 --> 00:37:36,882
LEVEL/SCORE, L1, L2, 950, L1

434
00:37:36,965 --> 00:37:39,760
I don't see why she'd go out of her way
to work for APPELLO.

435
00:37:42,721 --> 00:37:47,809
CEO, you don't think she's a corporate spy
sent by Director Kim, do you?

436
00:37:47,893 --> 00:37:50,020
From what I've heard, that guy...

437
00:37:50,103 --> 00:37:53,398
has taken over countless companies
by planting spies.

438
00:37:56,568 --> 00:37:58,695
Let's keep a close eye on her for now.

439
00:38:00,364 --> 00:38:03,575
2025 E-COMMERCE LEADERS MEET-UP

440
00:38:13,544 --> 00:38:15,003
You have to admit,
APPELLO is really smart.

441
00:38:15,712 --> 00:38:17,965
While everyone was busy trying
to recruit famous designers,

442
00:38:18,048 --> 00:38:19,508
they went after up-and-coming designers.

443
00:38:20,843 --> 00:38:21,927
It was Director Lee Chan's idea.

444
00:38:22,678 --> 00:38:25,055
He thought it was a shame that
talented brands were disappearing

445
00:38:25,138 --> 00:38:26,849
because they lacked distribution networks.

446
00:38:26,932 --> 00:38:29,017
So, did you two know each other
before all this?

447
00:38:29,101 --> 00:38:30,686
We were high school classmates.

448
00:38:30,769 --> 00:38:32,396
So you're best friends.

449
00:38:33,355 --> 00:38:34,815
No wonder you'd entrust the company
to him.

450
00:38:43,782 --> 00:38:45,993
Well, we'll be counting on you.

451
00:38:46,076 --> 00:38:48,829
It seems SE Corporation has now joined
the e-commerce business as well.

452
00:38:48,912 --> 00:38:51,415
We're scheduled to launch
a fashion platform soon.

453
00:38:51,665 --> 00:38:54,793
Oh, so you're competing with APPELLO?

454
00:38:55,544 --> 00:38:57,004
Oh, competition?

455
00:38:57,880 --> 00:38:59,798
That's for those in the same weight class.

456
00:39:00,674 --> 00:39:03,051
With our capital and distribution network,
if we don't take the number one spot,

457
00:39:03,135 --> 00:39:05,387
that would be stranger, wouldn't it?

458
00:39:10,642 --> 00:39:12,519
So you used investment as an excuse
to steal our data,

459
00:39:12,603 --> 00:39:13,979
afraid you couldn't become number one?

460
00:39:14,813 --> 00:39:16,356
I heard you've planted spies
and stolen secrets

461
00:39:16,440 --> 00:39:18,400
from more than just one or two companies.

462
00:39:18,483 --> 00:39:20,277
A spy?

463
00:39:20,944 --> 00:39:23,197
Then what about APPELLO?

464
00:39:23,280 --> 00:39:26,617
Do I have someone on the inside or not?

465
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,535
You're CEO Kang Ha-gi, aren't you?

466
00:40:10,869 --> 00:40:13,163
I'm Do Eun-yong reporter
from the Insight Economic Times.

467
00:40:14,831 --> 00:40:15,749
DO EUN-YONG, INSIGHT TIMES

468
00:40:15,832 --> 00:40:18,210
A pleasure.

469
00:40:18,293 --> 00:40:20,128
I look forward to favorable articles.

470
00:40:23,757 --> 00:40:26,218
You should make some time
for an interview.

471
00:40:26,301 --> 00:40:27,928
There's a lot I'm curious about.

472
00:40:28,011 --> 00:40:29,847
If you contact my office,
we can coordinate.

473
00:40:29,930 --> 00:40:32,558
I'm not interested in APPELLO.
I'm interested in you.

474
00:40:41,024 --> 00:40:45,153
- I'm here. See you in a bit.
- I'm sorry. Something's come up.

475
00:40:46,530 --> 00:40:47,531
Are you finished?

476
00:41:04,423 --> 00:41:05,716
Why are you so dressed up?

477
00:41:06,592 --> 00:41:09,595
- Did you put on cologne, too? Huh?
- Stop being so clingy.

478
00:41:09,678 --> 00:41:13,390
What? I'm just happy to see you.
It's been a while.

479
00:41:14,850 --> 00:41:17,436
You only call me when it's about work.

480
00:41:17,519 --> 00:41:19,605
Why are you at a hotel
when you have a perfectly good home?

481
00:41:20,314 --> 00:41:21,565
Someone keeps showing up.

482
00:41:23,442 --> 00:41:24,651
Be careful.

483
00:41:24,735 --> 00:41:27,738
- Don't be an owner risk.
- It's already over.

484
00:41:27,821 --> 00:41:29,573
She was in the same industry.

485
00:41:29,656 --> 00:41:30,908
Keep it that way.

486
00:41:33,035 --> 00:41:35,787
Only get involved with people
who have as much to lose as you do.

487
00:41:38,248 --> 00:41:41,168
That's our CEO Kang Ha-gi for you.

488
00:41:42,211 --> 00:41:44,087
This is why you haven't dated anyone
in ten years...

489
00:41:44,838 --> 00:41:48,509
No, wait. It's because you can't.
You're so cold.

490
00:41:48,592 --> 00:41:53,013
Hey, get a hobby.
Or get into some fan activity.

491
00:41:53,764 --> 00:41:55,390
I have a bias.

492
00:41:57,976 --> 00:42:00,187
You do? Who?

493
00:42:01,146 --> 00:42:04,566
- APPELLO.
- Yeah, yeah. I know.

494
00:42:04,650 --> 00:42:07,569
Your bias is me. Say it's me.

495
00:42:07,653 --> 00:42:10,113
Just say it's me. Say, 'Lee Chan'.

496
00:42:10,197 --> 00:42:12,741
- Say, 'My bias is Lee Chan.'
- APPELLO.

497
00:42:12,824 --> 00:42:14,451
Say, 'You're my bias.'

498
00:42:14,535 --> 00:42:16,036
- APPELLO.
- Lee Chan.

499
00:42:16,119 --> 00:42:17,538
- APPELLO.
- I'm gonna bite you.

500
00:42:17,621 --> 00:42:18,956
That explains it.

501
00:42:41,103 --> 00:42:43,355
- What's with her again?
- Just leave her.

502
00:42:43,438 --> 00:42:46,483
Hey, Da-reum! Come have some chicken!

503
00:42:46,567 --> 00:42:48,026
No!

504
00:42:48,110 --> 00:42:50,070
I'm not done yet!

505
00:42:57,619 --> 00:43:02,249
Hey, Mi-mi.
Can I just do another hundred of these?

506
00:43:02,332 --> 00:43:05,961
I need to tire myself out so I don't think
about what happened in the CEO's office...

507
00:43:07,171 --> 00:43:10,299
Great, it came back to me again.

508
00:43:10,382 --> 00:43:13,010
What are you worried about?
Things like that happen.

509
00:43:13,093 --> 00:43:14,636
No.

510
00:43:16,388 --> 00:43:19,808
Hey, how am I supposed
to face the CEO now?

511
00:43:20,475 --> 00:43:23,020
And what about being
the weird girl at work?

512
00:43:27,441 --> 00:43:28,483
It's just your first day.

513
00:43:28,567 --> 00:43:30,444
Just focus on doing a good job
from now on.

514
00:43:30,527 --> 00:43:32,446
That'll make the rumors go away.

515
00:43:33,989 --> 00:43:36,325
- You think so?
- Of course.

516
00:43:36,408 --> 00:43:39,620
Besides, you're just a new employee.
How often will you even see the CEO?

517
00:43:39,703 --> 00:43:41,038
Just avoid him.

518
00:43:42,539 --> 00:43:43,540
Right?

519
00:43:45,042 --> 00:43:50,214
I probably won't have
to see the CEO, right?

520
00:43:51,298 --> 00:43:54,134
- Probably not.
- Nope.

521
00:43:54,218 --> 00:43:57,262
Whew. Right. I won't.

522
00:43:57,346 --> 00:43:58,847
I won't. I won't.

523
00:44:02,559 --> 00:44:07,064
I just need to work hard and fix my image.
And the CEO...

524
00:44:07,147 --> 00:44:07,981
I'll just avoid him.

525
00:44:08,774 --> 00:44:09,775
Yes!

526
00:44:11,318 --> 00:44:13,111
APPELLO X TUNZI POP-UP/SHOWROOM
OPENS IN NOVEMBER

527
00:44:19,159 --> 00:44:21,745
This is our first pop-up
since launching TUNZI,

528
00:44:21,828 --> 00:44:23,705
so let's all make sure
we're well prepared.

529
00:44:23,789 --> 00:44:24,998
Yes!

530
00:44:46,019 --> 00:44:47,020
I'll do it!

531
00:44:57,614 --> 00:44:58,615
Let me help you with that!

532
00:45:06,206 --> 00:45:07,875
I'll take that.

533
00:45:22,598 --> 00:45:23,640
TUNZI OUTFIT SETUP LIST

534
00:45:48,707 --> 00:45:49,917
Doors closing.

535
00:45:53,921 --> 00:45:57,341
Work hard and avoid the CEO.

536
00:46:12,564 --> 00:46:14,191
Doors closing.

537
00:46:17,778 --> 00:46:21,156
Hello! We're the new employees.
I'm Nam Da-reum,

538
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:23,033
- Park Youngwoo,
- and Lee Min-a!

539
00:46:23,116 --> 00:46:24,576
We look forward to working with you!

540
00:46:26,370 --> 00:46:28,038
- They're cute.
- They have good energy.

541
00:46:28,121 --> 00:46:29,456
- Alright, cheers.
- Okay, okay.

542
00:46:29,540 --> 00:46:31,416
Cheers!

543
00:46:31,500 --> 00:46:34,169
We'll do our best!

544
00:46:34,253 --> 00:46:37,339
Cheers! Cheers!

545
00:46:37,422 --> 00:46:42,386
Cheers! We'll do our best!

546
00:46:43,762 --> 00:46:45,013
Thank you.

547
00:47:11,915 --> 00:47:14,835
Make way for CEO Kang Ha-gi!

548
00:47:21,592 --> 00:47:23,427
Hello, CEO!

549
00:47:23,510 --> 00:47:25,220
Hello, CEO.

550
00:47:25,304 --> 00:47:27,556
- Please have a seat.
- CEO, please sit here.

551
00:47:27,639 --> 00:47:30,601
No, no. Why here? Why this seat?

552
00:47:34,438 --> 00:47:35,314
Please sit.

553
00:47:38,817 --> 00:47:41,778
- I thought you were too busy to make it.
- I have to leave soon.

554
00:47:41,862 --> 00:47:42,779
I have a video meeting
with an overseas VC.

555
00:47:42,863 --> 00:47:45,616
- CEO, would you like a drink?
- A video conference.

556
00:47:45,699 --> 00:47:48,160
That's right. Yes.

557
00:47:48,243 --> 00:47:49,828
Help yourselves.

558
00:47:51,163 --> 00:47:55,876
What's wrong? Why the somber mood?
Come on, everyone! Drink up! Huh?

559
00:47:55,959 --> 00:47:58,295
Our CEO is here,
so let's get this party...

560
00:47:58,378 --> 00:48:02,382
- Let's liven things up! Bottoms up!
- Bottoms up!

561
00:48:02,466 --> 00:48:04,301
Um, CEO. You're not drinking?

562
00:48:04,968 --> 00:48:07,846
- Please teach us well.
- We'll learn a lot from you.

563
00:48:12,267 --> 00:48:13,685
Let's wrap this up early today.

564
00:48:14,603 --> 00:48:15,896
Don't make the new hires drink too much.

565
00:48:15,979 --> 00:48:17,439
Okay.

566
00:48:22,152 --> 00:48:25,447
Da-reum has a company dinner tonight,
and I'm worried sick.

567
00:48:25,531 --> 00:48:27,616
She doesn't know how to say no
and accepts every drink.

568
00:48:27,699 --> 00:48:29,368
She's a born goody-two-shoes.

569
00:48:30,202 --> 00:48:31,703
Anyway, that Da-reum...

570
00:48:32,538 --> 00:48:34,790
Her problem is that she tries too hard.

571
00:48:48,387 --> 00:48:50,055
- Man, seriously.
- Manager, have a drink.

572
00:48:50,138 --> 00:48:51,974
Me? Me, me, me, me? Me, me, me.

573
00:48:53,517 --> 00:48:55,561
Wow, Da-reum. I didn't know
you had this hidden talent.

574
00:48:55,644 --> 00:48:57,396
Oh, my friends taught me.

575
00:48:57,479 --> 00:49:00,566
You've got good friends.
Hold on a second, sweetie.

576
00:49:01,817 --> 00:49:03,235
You have to accept my drink.

577
00:49:03,318 --> 00:49:04,611
Okay.

578
00:49:04,695 --> 00:49:07,114
- Here you go.
- Ms. Nam Da-reum.

579
00:49:07,197 --> 00:49:09,157
Yes?

580
00:49:09,241 --> 00:49:10,784
Have a drink from me instead.

581
00:49:11,827 --> 00:49:14,288
Yes!

582
00:49:14,371 --> 00:49:16,456
- But...
- Yes.

583
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:18,917
Use that glass.

584
00:49:19,751 --> 00:49:21,211
Yes.

585
00:49:22,254 --> 00:49:23,589
Okay.

586
00:49:29,344 --> 00:49:30,304
These dinners are optional.

587
00:49:31,597 --> 00:49:32,890
You can go home early if you're tired.

588
00:49:35,559 --> 00:49:37,477
Yes, I understand.

589
00:50:08,967 --> 00:50:13,138
Maybe I should go recharge for a bit.

590
00:50:20,646 --> 00:50:21,647
Bottoms up, bottoms up!

591
00:50:22,564 --> 00:50:24,274
It's almost time for my meeting,
so I'll be leaving now.

592
00:50:24,358 --> 00:50:26,318
Yes, you should get going, CEO.

593
00:50:27,444 --> 00:50:29,279
Take care, CEO.

594
00:50:50,592 --> 00:50:51,802
Why is Director Kim here...?

595
00:51:05,607 --> 00:51:06,942
Damn it...

596
00:51:41,810 --> 00:51:46,690
If I keep working hard, someday...

597
00:51:49,276 --> 00:51:52,696
I'll be able to see it for real, right?

598
00:51:59,328 --> 00:52:02,539
But this looks amazing.

599
00:52:04,082 --> 00:52:06,084
I have to take a picture.

600
00:52:06,168 --> 00:52:07,419
Where is it?

601
00:52:15,719 --> 00:52:17,221
Why isn't it working?

602
00:52:18,388 --> 00:52:21,308
Zero, nine, one, six.

603
00:52:24,561 --> 00:52:27,147
But that's his birthday.

604
00:52:27,231 --> 00:52:31,693
Zero, nine, one...

605
00:52:43,163 --> 00:52:44,706
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

606
00:52:44,790 --> 00:52:45,791
Yes?

607
00:52:46,458 --> 00:52:48,627
What are you doing here right now?

608
00:52:50,587 --> 00:52:53,298
- CEO?
- Why are you here and not at the dinner?

609
00:52:53,382 --> 00:52:54,758
Huh?

610
00:52:54,842 --> 00:52:56,552
Me? Me?

611
00:52:57,219 --> 00:52:58,720
I...

612
00:52:58,804 --> 00:53:02,391
Oh, I was just trying to recharge a bit.

613
00:53:02,474 --> 00:53:05,686
- Recharge?
- But you said...

614
00:53:07,062 --> 00:53:10,357
...I'm always welcome.
That the CEO's office door is

615
00:53:11,316 --> 00:53:13,610
always open.

616
00:53:14,653 --> 00:53:15,487
And...

617
00:53:16,446 --> 00:53:17,406
...a picture.

618
00:53:18,115 --> 00:53:23,579
I was just going to take
one quick picture and leave.

619
00:53:24,746 --> 00:53:26,290
What picture?

620
00:53:41,180 --> 00:53:44,099
All right! Okay, everyone!
Attention, attention!

621
00:53:44,892 --> 00:53:47,895
It's a rite of passage for every
new employee at our company.

622
00:53:47,978 --> 00:53:49,855
- Oh, that?
- Yes.

623
00:53:49,938 --> 00:53:52,107
Now, for our dear Lee Min-a...

624
00:53:52,191 --> 00:53:55,944
Will it be CEO Ha-gi's faction,
or Director Chan's Faction?

625
00:53:56,028 --> 00:53:57,654
Excuse me?

626
00:53:57,738 --> 00:54:00,490
Team CEO Ha-gi, who's dependable
but a bit prickly,

627
00:54:00,574 --> 00:54:03,410
hard on the outside, soft on the inside?
Or Team Director Chan,

628
00:54:03,493 --> 00:54:06,330
who looks like he walked straight out
of a comic book?

629
00:54:07,748 --> 00:54:12,294
Oh, um, I feel a little put on the spot...

630
00:54:12,377 --> 00:54:15,172
Well, if you're that uncomfortable,
there's always Team Jin-sang.

631
00:54:16,006 --> 00:54:18,550
- You can join.
- What?

632
00:54:18,634 --> 00:54:20,344
- Hey, don't ruin the mood.
- What?

633
00:54:20,427 --> 00:54:21,845
Hurry up and pick one.

634
00:54:21,929 --> 00:54:24,223
Then I choose...

635
00:54:29,895 --> 00:54:32,147
Team CEO Ha-gi?

636
00:54:36,360 --> 00:54:39,488
- Min-a, nice! I'm on Team Ha-gi too.
- I knew it would be Ha-gi.

637
00:54:39,571 --> 00:54:41,365
Why is everyone on Team Ha-gi?

638
00:55:08,642 --> 00:55:11,144
Did she really come in here
drunk or something?

639
00:55:20,195 --> 00:55:24,199
CEO Kang, that was a
very impressive presentation.

640
00:55:24,283 --> 00:55:27,035
Well, Mr. Kang. APPELLO's growth is great,

641
00:55:27,119 --> 00:55:28,662
Your platform's growth metrics
are outstanding.

642
00:55:28,745 --> 00:55:32,040
Above all, the "Unframe" philosophy,
and the Unframe philosophy?

643
00:55:33,792 --> 00:55:35,752
It's an excellent differentiator
in a very competitive market.

644
00:55:35,836 --> 00:55:38,589
In what is a very crowded market.

645
00:55:38,672 --> 00:55:41,592
Our team will be in touch within the week,
to discuss the next steps.

646
00:55:42,384 --> 00:55:43,760
It's a pleasure, Mr. Kang.

647
00:55:43,844 --> 00:55:45,637
- A pleasure, CEO Kang.
- Thank you. Thank you.

648
00:55:45,721 --> 00:55:48,432
- I hope to see you again soon.
- You bet. Of course. Take care.

649
00:56:26,094 --> 00:56:27,304
She didn't hear that, right?

650
00:56:33,936 --> 00:56:35,354
Nam Da-reum.

651
00:56:48,492 --> 00:56:49,826
Nam Da-reum, it's time to go home.

652
00:56:50,702 --> 00:56:52,871
Wake up. Nam Da-reum.

653
00:57:08,762 --> 00:57:10,347
This is driving me nuts.

654
00:57:12,891 --> 00:57:13,892
What do I do?

655
00:57:39,334 --> 00:57:40,335
Huh?

656
00:57:50,596 --> 00:57:51,597
This is crazy.

657
00:57:53,849 --> 00:57:55,309
I must be crazy.

658
00:57:56,560 --> 00:57:58,312
I'm crazy!

659
00:58:02,441 --> 00:58:03,650
Oh, seriously.

660
00:58:09,406 --> 00:58:10,574
I think I'm going to throw up.

661
00:58:20,334 --> 00:58:23,712
What? You and the CEO did...

662
00:58:27,633 --> 00:58:30,385
- You slept with him?
- No!

663
00:58:30,469 --> 00:58:35,098
No, I fell asleep in the CEO's office.

664
00:58:38,852 --> 00:58:40,812
Right, there is no way
my confucian girl would do that.

665
00:58:41,730 --> 00:58:42,981
But why on earth did you go there?

666
00:58:45,734 --> 00:58:46,610
I do not know.

667
00:58:47,277 --> 00:58:48,654
I think I went into zombie mode again.

668
00:58:49,530 --> 00:58:51,448
There is a picture of Chan in there.

669
00:58:51,532 --> 00:58:55,827
- Not a photoshoot, a natural one.
- You are nuts.

670
00:58:56,537 --> 00:58:59,665
Please, get a handle
on that drinking habit. For real.

671
00:58:59,748 --> 00:59:01,959
Da-reum, I'm telling you
because you make things so hard for me.

672
00:59:02,835 --> 00:59:06,380
I'm sorry.
I'm really not drinking anymore, for real.

673
00:59:06,463 --> 00:59:07,464
Good grief!

674
00:59:10,926 --> 00:59:13,136
But you didn't cause more trouble
in the CEO's office, right?

675
00:59:14,012 --> 00:59:14,930
Probably...

676
00:59:15,722 --> 00:59:16,932
I guess so?

677
00:59:19,393 --> 00:59:21,186
What... I have a bad feeling about this.

678
00:59:21,270 --> 00:59:23,397
- I don't know.
- Don't tell me, you...

679
00:59:24,857 --> 00:59:25,816
Did you black out?

680
00:59:27,150 --> 00:59:28,151
Yeah.

681
00:59:32,322 --> 00:59:33,949
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

682
00:59:34,032 --> 00:59:36,201
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

683
00:59:50,090 --> 00:59:54,178
Whoa, Nam Da-reum!
Hey, I saw a new side of you yesterday.

684
00:59:54,261 --> 00:59:56,346
You just took this,
went like this, and pop!

685
00:59:56,430 --> 01:00:02,186
The bottle cap spun right off,
flew over there, and bam!

686
01:00:02,269 --> 01:00:04,146
One of a kind.

687
01:00:04,855 --> 01:00:06,899
- High-five.
- Huh?

688
01:00:06,982 --> 01:00:10,152
M-me? What did I do? Why...

689
01:00:13,113 --> 01:00:15,115
What's going on?

690
01:00:15,199 --> 01:00:17,159
- Da-reum, you were so cool yesterday.
- Huh?

691
01:00:17,242 --> 01:00:18,076
Da-reum, you're the best.

692
01:00:29,379 --> 01:00:31,131
Good morning!

693
01:00:31,215 --> 01:00:32,216
Good morning.

694
01:00:37,846 --> 01:00:38,889
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

695
01:00:38,972 --> 01:00:40,015
Did you get home okay?

696
01:00:40,641 --> 01:00:42,351
You seemed drunk when you left early.

697
01:00:42,434 --> 01:00:43,685
Yes.

698
01:00:51,860 --> 01:00:55,113
- He's so handsome.
- Nam Da-reum.

699
01:00:55,197 --> 01:00:57,407
Nam Da-reum.

700
01:00:58,700 --> 01:01:00,786
What? What is this memory?

701
01:01:00,869 --> 01:01:02,996
I think the CEO was there.

702
01:01:04,248 --> 01:01:05,749
Um, Team Leader.

703
01:01:05,832 --> 01:01:09,545
- Yes?
- Has the CEO come in?

704
01:01:09,628 --> 01:01:10,712
The CEO?

705
01:01:10,796 --> 01:01:12,756
I think he stayed up all night
at the office again.

706
01:01:12,840 --> 01:01:14,091
He did?

707
01:01:21,765 --> 01:01:23,851
Shoot, what's going on?

708
01:01:23,934 --> 01:01:26,270
What could have happened
for him to be looking at me?

709
01:01:26,353 --> 01:01:30,065
Remember, please. Think, think, think.
Come on, Da-reum.

710
01:01:30,190 --> 01:01:31,817
SAMPLE ROOM

711
01:01:44,162 --> 01:01:45,998
Hey, looks like someone's still hungover.

712
01:01:46,874 --> 01:01:49,459
Da-reum. Oh, there you are.

713
01:01:49,543 --> 01:01:51,461
- Are you feeling okay?
- Yes.

714
01:01:52,754 --> 01:01:54,715
I was really drunk yesterday, wasn't I?

715
01:01:54,798 --> 01:01:58,177
- I didn't make mistakes yesterday, did I?
- Huh? Mistakes?

716
01:01:58,260 --> 01:02:00,345
Mistakes? What mistakes? You left early,
what mistakes could you have made?

717
01:02:00,429 --> 01:02:05,267
Oh, Da-reum. It's too bad you couldn't
stay longer yesterday.

718
01:02:05,350 --> 01:02:08,562
I mean, Director Lee Chan
even came at the end,

719
01:02:08,645 --> 01:02:10,814
and it was incredible.

720
01:02:10,898 --> 01:02:12,065
What?

721
01:02:12,941 --> 01:02:14,234
Whoa, what a surprise.

722
01:02:14,318 --> 01:02:16,612
I mean, I thought
he was just good-looking,

723
01:02:16,695 --> 01:02:19,698
but his personality is great too.
Look. He took a picture just with us

724
01:02:19,781 --> 01:02:21,533
to congratulate us
for joining the company.

725
01:02:26,330 --> 01:02:27,706
Chan came?

726
01:02:29,625 --> 01:02:33,337
But, um... here at the company,
he's Director...

727
01:02:33,420 --> 01:02:36,882
Shouldn't you call him Director?

728
01:02:37,841 --> 01:02:40,469
Wait a minute.
I guess Da-reum is a fan of DNX.

729
01:02:40,552 --> 01:02:41,678
- Right?
- Oh.

730
01:02:41,762 --> 01:02:43,430
I mean, I almost made the mistake
of just saying,

731
01:02:43,514 --> 01:02:44,723
"It's Lee Chan!" yesterday too.

732
01:02:45,474 --> 01:02:47,100
Oh my.

733
01:02:47,184 --> 01:02:48,936
Da-reum, what's wrong?

734
01:02:49,019 --> 01:02:50,771
Is it because of what I said?

735
01:02:54,608 --> 01:02:55,609
No, it's not.

736
01:02:57,110 --> 01:02:58,237
It's nothing.

737
01:03:09,373 --> 01:03:10,541
Getting drunk...

738
01:03:12,125 --> 01:03:14,002
Crawling into the CEO's office to sleep.

739
01:03:16,755 --> 01:03:18,215
I didn't even get to see Chan.

740
01:03:24,346 --> 01:03:25,973
What's the point of living, Nam Da-reum?

741
01:03:27,808 --> 01:03:29,434
Just die. Just drop dead.

742
01:03:30,644 --> 01:03:34,606
It was finally my chance to see him.

743
01:04:19,151 --> 01:04:20,861
Yikes!

744
01:04:23,614 --> 01:04:24,615
Ms. Nam Da-reum,

745
01:04:24,698 --> 01:04:26,658
why do you call for your mom
when you see me?

746
01:04:27,534 --> 01:04:29,828
Um, about yesterday...

747
01:04:31,580 --> 01:04:33,957
I'm sorry, CEO.

748
01:04:34,041 --> 01:04:37,377
I remember getting drunk
and going into your office,

749
01:04:37,461 --> 01:04:39,546
but when I woke up, it was morning.

750
01:04:42,925 --> 01:04:44,593
You don't remember?

751
01:04:45,761 --> 01:04:47,804
How convenient
that you never seem to remember.

752
01:04:49,181 --> 01:04:51,475
- What?
- Never mind.

753
01:04:51,558 --> 01:04:52,768
It's probably for the best.

754
01:04:53,894 --> 01:04:55,521
I was going to send you home
once you sobered up,

755
01:04:55,604 --> 01:04:57,189
but you were too drunk to wake up.

756
01:04:57,272 --> 01:04:58,649
Then,

757
01:04:59,274 --> 01:05:00,943
what about you, CEO?

758
01:05:03,403 --> 01:05:04,780
I...

759
01:05:07,616 --> 01:05:09,076
I left after working.

760
01:05:10,577 --> 01:05:13,580
Of course. What a relief.

761
01:05:13,664 --> 01:05:14,748
I was worried I kept you from leaving.

762
01:05:14,831 --> 01:05:18,085
Please be more careful in the future.
Behavior like that...

763
01:05:18,168 --> 01:05:20,045
can give people the wrong idea.

764
01:05:21,547 --> 01:05:22,464
Yes.

765
01:05:22,548 --> 01:05:26,260
I'm sorry, CEO.
I'll make sure it never happens again.

766
01:05:33,600 --> 01:05:34,476
Yes, Team Leader.

767
01:05:34,560 --> 01:05:37,938
Da-reum, go to the first-floor showroom
and help them tidy up.

768
01:05:38,105 --> 01:05:39,356
Yes, yes.

769
01:05:41,066 --> 01:05:43,151
My team leader told me
to go to the showroom,

770
01:05:43,235 --> 01:05:45,195
so I should get going.

771
01:05:54,454 --> 01:05:55,622
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

772
01:06:00,460 --> 01:06:01,670
What? Why is he following me?

773
01:06:14,975 --> 01:06:17,102
The miracle I'd hoped for desperately...

774
01:06:19,104 --> 01:06:20,856
didn't happen on a special day,

775
01:06:23,066 --> 01:06:25,694
but in the middle of a very ordinary one.

776
01:06:28,614 --> 01:06:31,533
At a totally unexpected moment.

777
01:07:05,859 --> 01:07:09,655
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

778
01:07:20,541 --> 01:07:21,500
CHEON SEON-AE

779
01:07:21,583 --> 01:07:23,544
EPILOGUE

780
01:08:07,921 --> 01:08:10,632
Scrub, with love.

781
01:08:10,716 --> 01:08:13,677
Scrub the grime from the heart.

782
01:08:13,760 --> 01:08:17,598
Even the grime in every corner.

783
01:08:17,681 --> 01:08:21,018
I'll scrub it away for you.

784
01:08:21,685 --> 01:08:25,230
Scrub, scrub. With love.

785
01:08:25,314 --> 01:08:28,609
The bruises on your heart...

786
01:08:29,318 --> 01:08:32,446
even the bruises on your heart,

787
01:08:32,588 --> 01:08:37,718
I will scrub away with love.

788
01:08:37,743 --> 01:08:39,578
Scrub, scrub.

789
01:08:39,603 --> 01:08:42,020
- Oh my, CEO!
- Um...

790
01:08:42,497 --> 01:08:46,835
- No, good morning, ma'am.
- My, you pulled an all-nighter again?

791
01:08:46,860 --> 01:08:48,962
- Go get some sleep.
- No...

792
01:08:49,046 --> 01:08:51,131
I'll be done in a flash.

793
01:08:55,302 --> 01:08:59,056
No, it's all right.
I have papers spread out everywhere.

794
01:08:59,139 --> 01:09:03,243
Goodness, don't mind me.

795
01:09:03,268 --> 01:09:07,064
If you still have work to do, go ahead.
I'll be out of your hair in a jiffy.

796
01:09:08,607 --> 01:09:11,693
- Huh?
- Ma-Ma'am.

797
01:09:12,653 --> 01:09:15,531
Ma-Ma'am, ma'am, Ms. Cheon!

798
01:09:16,240 --> 01:09:17,449
Would you...

799
01:09:18,534 --> 01:09:20,536
like to have a cup of coffee with me?

800
01:09:20,619 --> 01:09:23,997
Coffee? A morning coffee sounds great.

801
01:09:24,790 --> 01:09:28,085
Scrub, scrub, scrub, scrub.
Scrub the grime.

802
01:09:35,217 --> 01:09:37,302
- Nice to meet you, Da-reum.
- How do you know my name?

803
01:09:37,386 --> 01:09:38,804
This isn't a dream, is it?

804
01:09:39,888 --> 01:09:41,640
Overseas Training for Top Employees?

805
01:09:42,266 --> 01:09:44,852
I get the sense
she's intentionally getting close to me.

806
01:09:44,935 --> 01:09:48,689
CEO, oh my. CEO, you're amazing.

807
01:09:48,772 --> 01:09:53,151
You don't think she's a honey trap
sent by Director Kim, do you?

808
01:09:53,235 --> 01:09:56,238
- Call me.
- See you!

809
01:09:56,822 --> 01:10:00,033
Are they dating? Our CEO and Chan?

810
01:10:00,117 --> 01:10:02,786
No way!

